STEP-BY-STEP SOLVING METHOD (OUTLINE):

1) Parsing and Clause Setup:
   • Convert each parenthesized triplet into a clause of three literals (possibly negated).

2) Initialization:
   • No immediate unit clauses or pure literals are found, so no immediate simplifications apply.

3) DPLL Search Process:
   • Choose a literal (e.g., x1) and branch by setting x1 = True.
   • Propagate consequences (unit propagation).  
   • If a contradiction (empty clause) is derived, backtrack, set x1 = False, and repeat.

4) Continuing Branching:
   • Systematically iterate through further unassigned variables (x2, x3, …) in a chosen heuristic order.
   • Each time a literal assignment implies new unit propagations, apply them.
   • On conflict, backtrack to the last branching decision and flip the assignment.

5) Exhaustive Exploration:
   • Because of repeated conflicts at different levels of the search tree, all possible assignments are eventually tried under backtracking.

6) Conclusion:
   • The search uncovers a conflict in every branch, indicating no complete satisfying assignment can be found.

